.\" No version in the title line: see the note in irontile.1.
.TH IRONTILE-BAR 1 "" "irontile" "irontile"
.SH NAME
irontile\-bar \- a status bar for irontile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B irontile\-bar
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B irontile\-bar \-\-dump
.I PATH
.RB [ \-\-width
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-scale
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-tooltip
.IR TEXT ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B irontile\-bar
is an ordinary layer\-shell client with no special access to the compositor: it
opens one bar per display, reserves the space it occupies, and reads everything
it shows from the places anything else could read them. It is not started by
the compositor; put it in
.B [startup]
in the configuration file.
.PP
Its configuration follows waybar's shape, because that is what people are
porting from: three regions naming modules, and a table per module carrying its
format string, icons and thresholds.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read configuration from
.I PATH
instead of the usual place.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump " PATH"
Render one bar to a PNG and exit, without a compositor. The quickest way to see
what a configuration looks like.
.TP
.BI \-\-width " N"
Width to render for
.BR \-\-dump .
Default 1200.
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " N"
Display scale to render for
.BR \-\-dump .
Default 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-tooltip " TEXT"
Render a tooltip saying
.I TEXT
rather than a bar, so the
.B [tooltip]
settings can be seen. Newlines are written
.BR \en .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a usage message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/irontile/bar.toml
Configuration. Falls back to
.IR ~/.config/irontile/bar.toml .
A missing file means the defaults.
.SH NOTES
Icons are named by the freedesktop specification and resolved against an
installed icon theme, so the names hold still across releases in a way a font's
codepoints do not. With no theme installed the bar draws its text and skips the
icons; with no font installed at all it cannot draw anything, which is why the
packages depend on one.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR irontile (1),
.BR irontilectl (1)
